<!--
  v6.4 — THE FLAG OF IRAN: THE LION AND SUN (شیر و خورشید).

  HARD PRODUCT RULE (from the brief, non-negotiable):
    "The real flag of Iran is the Lion and Sun flag. Even if the internet is
     weak, instead of the Islamic-Republic flag it MUST show the real flag of
     Iran — the Lion and Sun. Under no circumstances may the Islamic-Republic
     flag be displayed anywhere in the app."

  Why this file exists at all:
    Everywhere else the app paints a country flag as a Unicode regional-indicator
    emoji pair, because that costs nothing and never lags. But the system font's
    "IR" emoji is the Islamic-Republic flag, which this app must never show. The
    ONLY way to guarantee the correct flag on every device, offline, with no
    network and no font dependency, is to draw it ourselves — which is what this
    vector does. It is rendered by CountryFlags/FlagView whenever the resolved
    country is IR, and the "IR" emoji is never emitted.

  Composition (classic tricolour, 3:2, Lion-and-Sun centred on the white band):
    • top band     — green   (#239F40)
    • middle band  — white,  carrying the emblem
    • bottom band  — red     (#DA0000)
    • emblem       — golden lion passant holding a sword, with the radiant sun
                     rising behind it, all in gold (#C8A02D / #E8B931).

  Drawn on a 90x60 viewport (3:2) so it scales cleanly into the square flag tile
  without distortion (the tile letterboxes it, see FlagView).
-->
